# Petal — environment
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (already git-ignored) and fill in both values.
# Full walkthrough: supabase/README.md
#
# Leave them out and the app runs on the seeded offline mock adapter — every
# screen works, nothing touches the network. Fill them in and `data/index.ts`
# switches to the live Supabase adapter automatically. That switch is the only
# one there is.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` values are INLINED INTO THE BUNDLE at build time. Two
# consequences worth remembering:
#   1. Changing them needs `npx expo start --clear` — a warm Metro cache keeps
#      serving the old values, which looks exactly like "my credentials are wrong".
#   2. Anything with this prefix ships to the device and is readable. Only the
#      anon/publishable key belongs here. The `service_role` key bypasses every
#      RLS policy in supabase/migrations/0002_rls.sql — it must never leave a
#      server.

# Project Settings → API → Project URL
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Project Settings → API → Project API keys → anon / publishable
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
